msgid "3.2 Change via a launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:347
msgid ""
"You can also set the parameter in a launch file, but first you will need to "
"add the launch directory. Inside the ``ros2_ws/src/cpp_parameters/`` "
"directory, create a new directory called ``launch``. In there, create a new "
"file called ``cpp_parameters_launch.py``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:352
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"from launch_ros.actions import Node\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    return LaunchDescription([\n"
"        Node(\n"
"            package='cpp_parameters',\n"
"            executable='minimal_param_node',\n"
"            name='custom_minimal_param_node',\n"
"            output='screen',\n"
"            emulate_tty=True,\n"
"            parameters=[\n"
"                {'my_parameter': 'earth'}\n"
"            ]\n"
"        )\n"
"    ])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:355
msgid ""
"Here you can see that we set ``my_parameter`` to ``earth`` when we launch "
"our node ``minimal_param_node``. By adding the two lines below, we ensure "
"our output is printed in our console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:358
msgid ""
"output=\"screen\",\n"
"emulate_tty=True,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:363
msgid ""
"Now open the ``CMakeLists.txt`` file. Below the lines you added earlier, add "
"the following lines of code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:366
msgid ""
"install(\n"
"  DIRECTORY launch\n"
"  DESTINATION share/${PROJECT_NAME}\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:373
msgid ""
"Open a console and navigate to the root of your workspace, ``ros2_ws``, and "
"build your new package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:395
msgid "Then source the setup files in a new terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:417
msgid ""
"Now run the node using the launch file we have just created. The terminal "
"should return the following message the first time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:420
msgid ""
"$ ros2 launch cpp_parameters cpp_parameters_launch.py\n"
"[INFO] [custom_minimal_param_node]: Hello earth!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:425
msgid ""
"Further outputs should show  ``[INFO] [minimal_param_node]: Hello world!`` "
"every second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:428
msgid "3.3 Change via launch file loading parameters from YAML file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:430
msgid ""
"Instead of listing parameters and their values in launch file, you can "
"create a separate YAML file that will be loaded in launch file. Placing "
"parameters in a YAML file makes it easier to organize them, for example, by "
"assigning them to different namespaces. You can read more about it :ref:"
"`here <LoadingParametersFromYAMLFile>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:436
msgid ""
"While declaring, getting and setting parameter value inside your C++ node, "
"you should use dot as a separator between parameter's namespace and name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:439
msgid "3.4 Change via passing YAML file as an argument at node startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Using-Parameters-In-A-Class-CPP.rst:441
msgid ""
"Return to :ref:`tutorial about parameters <LoadParameterFileOnNodeStartup>` "
"to remind yourself, how to load parameters file at node startup using CLI."
msgstr ""

